		<title>King Promise’s “Melody” Is The Start Of A New Era</title>
		<link>https://thenativemag.com/king-promises-melody-is-the-start-of-a-new-era/</link>
					<comments>https://thenativemag.com/king-promises-melody-is-the-start-of-a-new-era/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Melony Akpoghene]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Music]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[king promise]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://thenativemag.com/?p=90266</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Sitting right at the intersection of Highlife, R&#038;B and mid-tempo Afropop, “Melody” stays straightforward and zeroes in on pure attraction.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://thenativemag.com/king-promises-melody-is-the-start-of-a-new-era/">King Promise’s “Melody” Is The Start Of A New Era</a> appeared first on <a href="https://thenativemag.com">The NATIVE</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ever since “</span><b>Terminator</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">” took over worldwide, Ghanaian artist King Promise has kept his foot on the gas, dropping constant heat while linking up with major names across music and football. Fresh off his joint tape ‘</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">See What We’ve Done</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">’ and a recent campaign with Chelsea FC, he is turning his focus back to his solo run with “</span><b>Melody</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">”, the first taste of his upcoming 2027 album.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Out today alongside its official music video, the record hits the exact sweet spot his fans expect. Sitting right at the intersection of Highlife, R&amp;B and mid-tempo Afropop, “</span><b>Melody</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">” stays straightforward and zeroes in on pure attraction. The main hook draws a direct line between a woman’s presence and a song stuck on repeat in your head.</span></p>
<p><iframe title="King Promise - Melody (Official Music Video)" width="640" height="480" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/T3kXs5CnMUA?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Following the release of ‘</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">As Promised</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">’ in 2019, King Promise has built a catalogue that moves between Ghanaian Pop and a wider Afropop audience. ‘</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">5 Star</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">’ (2022) and ‘</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">True to Self</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">’ (2024) expanded that run, while “</span><b>Terminator</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">” became his biggest international hit. His public profile has also taken him beyond music. This month, he worked with Chelsea FC on “</span><b>Can’t Tame Us</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">”, the club’s official anthem for its London to the World campaign. The accompanying football tournament in Accra brought the campaign to Nungua, where King Promise grew up playing the game and spotlighted his Rent Paid initiative, which connects young people in his community with the sport.</span></p>
<p><iframe title="King Promise - Can&#039;t Tame Us (Chelsea Anthem) (Official Audio)" width="640" height="360" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/j7-JiDdYKhc?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">“</span><b>Melody</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">” comes with King Promise working within a sound he knows well. Whether it signals a new direction for the forthcoming album remains to be heard; for now, the single keeps his attention on the pleasures of a well-made love song.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Listen to “<strong>Melody</strong>” </span><a href="https://us.list-manage.com/mTvwLt1UZ5i?e=ba214c122f&amp;c2id=40e259b745b3765a66131bdf3706fad4"><span style="font-weight: 400;">here</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://thenativemag.com/king-promises-melody-is-the-start-of-a-new-era/">King Promise’s “Melody” Is The Start Of A New Era</a> appeared first on <a href="https://thenativemag.com">The NATIVE</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
